{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:29:63-64","rows":[{"verses":["29:63"],"words":["فَأَحْيَا بِهِ ٱلْأَرْضَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Acknowledging that God sends rain and revives barren land should make people reject association and resurrection-denial; the same power can enrich believers.","anchor":"فإذا أقررتم بذلك فلم تشركون به وتنكرون الإعادة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:63"],"words":["قُلِ ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The command to praise God responds to the clear proofs of His power that He has shown.","anchor":"أي على ما أوضح من الحجج والبراهين على قدرته","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:63"],"words":["قُلِ ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"An alternative explanation takes the praise as being for the interlocutors’ acknowledgment that God sends rain and revives land.","anchor":"«الحمد لله» على إقرارهم بذلك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:63"],"words":["قُلِ ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"Another reported explanation takes the praise as being for sending water and bringing the earth back to life.","anchor":"وقيل: على إنزال الماء وإحياء الأرض","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:63"],"words":["بَلْ أَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْقِلُونَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Most people do not reflect on these proofs of divine power.","anchor":"بل أكثرهم لا يعقلون } أي لا يتدبرون هذه الحجج","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:64"],"words":["وَمَا هَٰذِهِ ٱلْحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنْيَآ إِلَّا لَهْوٌۭ وَلَعِبٌۭ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Worldly life is diversion and play: wealth and status fade and have no enduring reality, like play that does not last.","anchor":"ليس ما أعطاه الله الأغنياء من الدنيا إلا وهو يضمحل ويزول كاللعب الذي لا حقيقة له ولا ثبات","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:64"],"words":["وَمَا هَٰذِهِ ٱلْحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنْيَآ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"This criticism concerns worldly wealth, status, and clothing beyond basic needs and the means needed to sustain life and obey God.","anchor":"الملبس الزائد على الضروري الذي به قوام العيش","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:64"],"words":["وَإِنَّ ٱلدَّارَ ٱلْءَاخِرَةَ لَهِىَ ٱلْحَيَوَانُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"What is done for God belongs to the afterlife and endures, meaning what is sought for His reward and pleasure.","anchor":"أي ما ابتغى به ثوابه ورضاه","mentions":["55:27"]},{"verses":["29:64"],"words":["وَإِنَّ ٱلدَّارَ ٱلْءَاخِرَةَ لَهِىَ ٱلْحَيَوَانُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The afterlife is the lasting abode of life: it does not pass away and contains no death.","anchor":"أي دار الحياة الباقية التي لا تزول ولا موت فيها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:64"],"words":["ٱلْحَيَوَانُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"أبو عبيدة","stance":"reports","claim":"Abu Ubayda equates al-ḥayawān with life and the word ḥayy with a kasra; an anonymous poetic line illustrates the usage of ḥayāt.","anchor":"وزعم أبو عبيدة: أن الحيوان والحياة والحي بكسر الحاء واحد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:64"],"words":["ٱلْحَيَوَانُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"غيره","stance":"reports","claim":"Others explain ḥayy as a plural on the pattern fuʿūl, like ʿuṣiyy.","anchor":"وغيره يقول: إن الحي جمع على فعول مثل عصي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:64"],"words":["ٱلْحَيَوَانُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The word al-ḥayawān can refer to any living thing.","anchor":"والحيوان يقع على كل شيء حي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:64"],"words":["ٱلْحَيَوَانُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The commentary also notes that Ḥayawān is the name of a spring in Paradise.","anchor":"وحيوان عين في الجنة. وقيل:","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:64"],"words":["ٱلْحَيَوَانُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"One derivation makes ḥayawān originally ḥayayyān, with one yāʾ changed to wāw where identical letters meet.","anchor":"وقيل: أصل حيوان حييان فأبدلت إحداهما واوا لاجتماع المثلين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:64"],"words":["لَوْ كَانُوا۟ يَعْلَمُونَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The closing clause means that they would know the afterlife is truly the enduring life if they understood.","anchor":"لو كانوا يعلمون } أنها كذلك","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:30:39","rows":[{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["وَمَآ ءَاتَيْتُم مِّن زَكَوٰةٍۢ تُرِيدُونَ وَجْهَ ٱللَّهِ"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"After mentioning what is done seeking God’s pleasure and reward, the passage turns to another kind of giving and then returns to what is sought for Him.","anchor":"لما ذكر ما يراد به وجهه ويثيب عليه ذكر غير ذلك من الصفة وما يراد به أيضا وجهه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["وَمَآ ءَاتَيْتُم مِّن رِّبًۭا"],"type":"readings","speaker":"الجمهور","stance":"reports","claim":"The majority read ātaytum with a long vowel, meaning ‘you gave.’","anchor":"قرأ الجمهور: «آتيتم» بالمد بمعنى أعطيتم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["لِّيَرْبُوَا۟ فِىٓ أَمْوَٰلِ ٱلنَّاسِ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"ابن كثير ومجاهد وحميد","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Kathir, Mujahid, and Humayd read without lengthening, meaning what you do of usury so it may increase.","anchor":"وقرأ ابن كثير ومجاهد وحميد بغير مد بمعنى ما فعلتم من ربا ليربو","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["وَمَآ ءَاتَيْتُم مِّن رِّبًۭا"],"type":"readings","speaker":"الجمهور","stance":"reports","claim":"All readers agree on the lengthened reading in the second phrase.","anchor":"وأجمعوا على المد في قوله: { ومآ آتيتم من ربا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["رِّبًۭا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Ribā means increase; the author contrasts forbidden usury discussed in al-Baqara with the permissible kind here, concluding there are lawful and unlawful forms.","anchor":"والربا الزيادة وقد مضى في «البقرة» معناه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟ فِىٓ أَمْوَٰلِ ٱلنَّاسِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"عكرمة","stance":"reports","claim":"Ikrima says ribā has a lawful and a forbidden kind; the lawful kind is a gift given in hope of receiving something better.","anchor":"قال عكرمة في قوله تعالى: { ومآ آتيتم من ربا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الضحاك","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Dahhak identifies the phrase with a lawful gift made in hope of a better return; it earns neither reward nor sin.","anchor":"وعن الضحاك في هذه الآية: هو الربا الحلال الذي يهدى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas says it means a gift offered in hope of a better return: its giver is not rewarded by God but is not sinful.","anchor":"وكذلك قال ابن عباس: «وما آتيتم من ربا» يريد هدية الرجل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس وابن جبير وطاوس ومجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas, Ibn Jubayr, Tawus, and Mujahid say the verse was revealed about gifts given expecting compensation.","anchor":"قال ابن عباس وابن جبير وطاوس ومجاهد: هذه آية نزلت في هبة الثواب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عطية","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Atiyya extends the point to acts such as greeting someone to obtain repayment: they incur no sin but earn no reward.","anchor":"قال ابن عطية: وما جرى مجراها مما يصنعه الإنسان ليجازى عليه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"القاضي أبو بكر بن العربي","stance":"reports","claim":"Qadi Abu Bakr ibn al-Arabi also adopts the view that such an act earns neither sin nor reward.","anchor":"لا أجر فيه ولا زيادة عند الله تعالى. وقاله القاضي أبو بكر بن العربي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عبد الرحمن بن علقمة","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Nasaʾi reports that the Thaqif delegation brought the Prophet a gift; he asked whether it was charity or a gift, explained the intentions, and accepted it as a gift.","anchor":"وفي كتاب النسائي عن عبد الرحمن بن علقمة قال","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس وإبراهيم النخعي","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas and Ibrahim al-Nakhaʿi say the verse concerns people who support relatives or brothers so they can benefit and grow wealthier.","anchor":"وقال ابن عباس أيضا وإبراهيم النخعي: نزلت في قوم يعطون قراباتهم وإخوانهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الشعبي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Shaʿbi explains it as serving someone lightly to gain worldly benefit; the service repaid in this life does not grow with God.","anchor":"وقال الشعبي: معنى الآية أن ما خدم الإنسان به أحدا وخف له","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"law","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"One view says the ban on giving to receive more applied specifically to the Prophet, citing the command not to give expecting an increase.","anchor":"وقيل: كان هذا حراما على النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم على الخصوص","mentions":["74:6"]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["فَلَا يَرْبُوا۟ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ"],"type":"law","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view identifies the phrase with forbidden usury and says the taker cannot claim it as his; it belongs to the person from whom it was taken.","anchor":"وقيل: إنه الربا المحرم فمعنى: «لا يربو عند الله» على هذا القول لا يحكم به لآخذه بل هو للمأخوذ منه.","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"reports","speaker":"السدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Suddi says the verse was revealed about usury practiced by Thaqif and by Quraysh against them.","anchor":"قال السدي: نزلت هذه الآية في ربا ثقيف لأنهم كانوا يعملون بالربا وتعمله فيهم قريش.","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:30:39#2","rows":[{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟ فِىٓ أَمْوَٰلِ ٱلنَّاسِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"القاضي أبو بكر بن العربي","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn al-Arabi says the verse expressly concerns someone who gives a gift seeking an increase from other people in return.","anchor":"قال القاضي أبو بكر بن العربي: صريح الآية فيمن يهب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The author says Ali's threefold classification of gifts is correct.","anchor":"الثالثة: ما ذكره علي رضي الله عنه وفصله من الهبة صحيح","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"law","speaker":"مالك","stance":"reports","claim":"Malik allows recompense when the giver is someone who normally expects it from the recipient, such as a poor person giving to a rich person; this is one Shafiʿi position.","anchor":"فقال مالك: ينظر فيه فإن كان مثله ممن يطلب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"law","speaker":"أبو حنيفة والشافعي","stance":"reports","claim":"Abu Hanifa and Shafiʿi's other position deny recompense without a condition; a gift for return is invalid because it resembles a sale for an unknown price.","anchor":"وقال أبو حنيفة: لا يكون له ثواب إذا لم يشترط","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"law","speaker":"الكوفي","stance":"reports","claim":"The Kufan argument is that imposing compensation destroys the gratuitous nature of a gift and turns it into an exchange.","anchor":"واحتج الكوفي بأن موضوع الهبة التبرع","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عمر بن الخطاب","stance":"reports","claim":"In Malik's Muwatta, Umar says a gift given with expectation of return remains the giver's until he is satisfied with the return.","anchor":"عن عمر بن الخطاب رضي الله عنه أنه قال: أيما رجل وهب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"reports","speaker":"علي","stance":"reports","claim":"Ali classifies gifts as intended for God, for people, or for recompense; the giver may reclaim the third kind if no recompense is given.","anchor":"عن علي رضي الله عنه قال: المواهب ثلاث","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عائشة","stance":"reports","claim":"Aisha reports that the Prophet accepted gifts and repaid them; he did not condemn a giver for seeking recompense, only resentment at a return above value.","anchor":"باب المكافأة في الهبة وساق حديث عائشة قالت","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:30:39#3","rows":[{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["وَمَآ ءَاتَيْتُم"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"The Prophet taught that deeds are judged by intentions and each person receives according to what he intended.","anchor":"الأعمال بالنيات وإنما لكل امرىء ما نوى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["تُرِيدُونَ وَجْهَ ٱللَّهِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"A gift intended for God's pleasure earns reward through His grace and mercy, as the verse promises multiplied reward.","anchor":"فأما إذا أراد بهبته وجه الله تعالى وابتغى عليه الثواب من عنده","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["تُرِيدُونَ وَجْهَ ٱللَّهِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Supporting a relative so they are not left dependent is judged by intention: worldly display is not for God, while fulfilling kinship rights is.","anchor":"وكذلك من يصل قرابته ليكون غنيا حتى لا يكون كلا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["تُرِيدُونَ وَجْهَ ٱللَّهِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"A gift made to win people's praise has no benefit or reward; the author links this to the warning against ostentatious charity.","anchor":"وأما من أراد بهبته وجوه الناس رياء ليحمدوه عليها","mentions":["2:264"]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"law","speaker":"ابن القاسم","stance":"reports","claim":"For a gift given expecting recompense, Ibn al-Qasim allows revocation until the recipient has repaid its value.","anchor":"ما لم يثب بقيمتها، على مذهب ابن القاسم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"law","speaker":"عمر وعلي","stance":"reports","claim":"On the apparent sense of Umar and Ali's statements, the giver may revoke until satisfied with a return greater than the gift's value.","anchor":"أو ما لم يرض منها بأزيد من قيمتها، على ظاهر قول عمر وعلي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"law","speaker":"مطرف","stance":"reports","claim":"Mutarrif's position in al-Wadihah permits revocation while the donated item remains, even if its value changed or the recipient gave more than its worth.","anchor":"وهو قول مطرف في الواضحة: أن الهبة ما كانت","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"law","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"Another view says that if the original gift remains unchanged, the giver may take whatever return he wants.","anchor":"وقد قيل: إنها إذا كانت قائمة العين لم تتغير","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"law","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"A further opinion requires the gift's value, comparing the case to a marriage in which the dowry was not stipulated.","anchor":"وقيل: تلزمه القيمة كنكاح التفويض","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["مِّن رِّبًۭا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"law","speaker":"ابن العربي","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn al-Arabi says that once the gift is no longer extant, only its value is owed, by agreement.","anchor":"ليس له إلا القيمة اتفاقا قاله ابن العربي","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:30:39#4","rows":[{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"readings","speaker":"جمهور القراء السبعة","stance":"reports","claim":"Most of the seven readers read li-yarbu with yāʾ, making the verb refer to ribā.","anchor":"قرأ جمهور القراء السبعة: «ليربو» بالياء وإسناد الفعل إلى الربا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"readings","speaker":"نافع وابن عباس والحسن وقتادة والشعبي","stance":"reports","claim":"Nafiʿ alone reads with tāʾ and a still wāw, addressing the plural as becoming people of increase; Ibn Abbas, Hasan, Qatada, and al-Shaʿbi also read it this way.","anchor":"قال أبو حاتم: هي قراءتنا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["لِّيَرْبُوَا۟"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أبو مالك","stance":"reports","claim":"Abu Malik reads liturbbūhā, with a feminine object pronoun.","anchor":"وقرأ أبو مالك: «لتربوها» بضمير مؤنث","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["فَلَا يَرْبُوا۟ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"This giving does not grow in purity or earn reward with God, who accepts only what is sincerely intended for Him.","anchor":"فلا يربوا عند الله } أي لا يزكوا ولا يثيب عليه لأنه لا يقبل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["زَكَوٰةٍۢ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas glosses zakāh here as charity.","anchor":"قال ابن عباس: أي من صدقة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلْمُضْعِفُونَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God accepts charity given for His pleasure and multiplies its reward tenfold or more, as in the cited verse about lending God a good loan.","anchor":"أي ذلك الذي يقبله ويضاعفه له عشرة أضعافه أو أكثر","mentions":["2:245"]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["تُرِيدُونَ وَجْهَ ٱللَّهِ"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The author also connects sincere spending for God's pleasure to the parable of a garden on a height.","anchor":"ومثل الذين ينفقون أموالهم ابتغاء مرضات الله وتثبيتا من أنفسهم","mentions":["2:265"]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["هُمُ ٱلْمُضْعِفُونَ"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The wording shifts from direct address to third person, as in the verse about being at sea and the ships moving with them.","anchor":"لأنه رجع من المخاطبة إلى الغيبة","mentions":["10:22"]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["هُمُ ٱلْمُضْعِفُونَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"One explanation is that their good deeds are multiplied; another is that they possess multiplied good and bliss.","anchor":"وفي معنى المضعفين قولان: أحدهما: أنه تضاعف لهم الحسنات","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["هُمُ ٱلْمُضْعِفُونَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Muqwin, musmin, and muʿaṭṭash describe someone whose camels are strong, fat, or thirsty; muḍʿaf can likewise describe one whose camels are weak.","anchor":"كما يقال: فلان مقو إذا كانت إبله قوية","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:39"],"words":["هُمُ ٱلْمُضْعِفُونَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The commentary uses the prophetic supplication's form mukhbith for one afflicted by impurity, contrasting one bad in himself with one whose companions are bad.","anchor":"فالمخبث: الذي أصابه خبث، يقال: فلان رديء أي هو رديء في نفسه","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:32:27","rows":[{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["أَنَّا نَسُوقُ ٱلْمَآءَ إِلَى ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The verse asks whether people recognize God's complete power in bringing water to lifeless, dry land and reviving it with crops.","anchor":"أي أولم يعلموا كمال قدرتنا بسوقنا الماء إلى الأرض اليابسة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الزمخشري","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Zamakhshari defines jarz land as land whose plants were cut away for lack of water or through grazing; salty flats are not called jarz.","anchor":"الزمخشري: الجرز الأرض التي جرز نباتها، أي قطع","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas identifies the jarz land as a region in Yemen.","anchor":"ابن عباس: هي أرض باليمن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujahid identifies it as Abyan.","anchor":"وقال مجاهد: هي أبين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"عكرمة","stance":"reports","claim":"Ikrima explains it as thirsty land.","anchor":"وقال عكرمة: هي الأرض الظمآى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الضحاك","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Dahhak calls it dead, thirsty land.","anchor":"وقال الضحاك: هي الأرض الميتة العطشى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farraʾ defines it as land with no vegetation.","anchor":"وقال الفراء: هي الأرض التي لا نبات فيها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الأصمعي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Asmaʿi defines it as land that grows nothing at all.","anchor":"وقال الأصمعي: هي الأرض التي لا تنبت شيئا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"محمد بن يزيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Muhammad ibn Yazid doubts that the word denotes a specific region because it has the definite article, though he allows such naming on the model of al-Abbas and al-Dahhak.","anchor":"وقال محمد بن يزيد: يبعد أن تكون لأرض بعينها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"prefers","claim":"The author favors allowing the Yemen identification: the Ibn Abbas transmission is sound, and jarz can be a descriptive adjective with the definite article.","anchor":"والإسناد عن ابن عباس صحيح لا مطعن فيه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The adjective derives from a man called jarūz, who leaves nothing uneaten; the cited rajaz line uses jarūz for such a voracious person.","anchor":"رجل جروز إذا كان لا يبقي شيئا إلا أكله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الفراء وغيره","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farraʾ and others report four vocalized forms for the word for jarz land, as with bukhl, raghb, and rahb.","anchor":"وحكى الفراء وغيره أنه يقال: أرض جرز وجرز","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A report says the land has no rivers and lies far from the sea; it receives a yearly Wadān, allowing three plantings yearly.","anchor":"وقد روي أن هذه الأرض لا أنهار فيها، وهي بعيدة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["ٱلْأَرْضِ ٱلْجُرُزِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujahid also identifies the land as the land of the Nile.","anchor":"وعن مجاهد أيضا: أنها أرض النيل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["فَنُخْرِجُ بِهِۦ زَرْعًۭا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The pronoun in ‘by it’ refers to the water.","anchor":"فنخرج به } أي بالماء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["تَأْكُلُ مِنْهُ أَنْعَٰمُهُمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Their livestock eat grasses and herbage from the crops, while people eat grains, greens, and fruits.","anchor":"تأكل منه أنعامهم } من الكلأ والحشيش","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["أَفَلَا يُبْصِرُونَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Seeing this revival should teach them that God has power to resurrect them.","anchor":"يبصرون } هذا فيعلمون أنا نقدر على إعادتهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["فَنُخْرِجُ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Fanukh'rij may coordinate with nasūq, or it may begin a new clause disconnected from what precedes.","anchor":"يكون معطوفا على «نسوق» أو منقطعا مما قبله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:27"],"words":["تَأْكُلُ مِنْهُ أَنْعَٰمُهُمْ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The clause taʾkulu minhu is in the accusative as an adjective describing the crop.","anchor":"في موضع نصب على النعت","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:33:41","rows":[{"verses":["33:41"],"words":["ٱذْكُرُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ ذِكْرًۭا كَثِيرًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God commands His servants to remember and thank Him abundantly; the command has no fixed limit because it is easy and its reward is great.","anchor":"أمر الله تعالى عباده بأن يذكروه ويشكروه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:41"],"words":["ذِكْرًۭا كَثِيرًۭا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas says no one is excused for neglecting remembrance of God except someone whose reason has been overcome.","anchor":"قال ابن عباس: لم يعذر أحد في ترك ذكر الله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:41"],"words":["ذِكْرًۭا كَثِيرًۭا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أبو سعيد والنبي","stance":"reports","claim":"Abu Saʿid reports that the Prophet urged people to remember God until others would call them mad.","anchor":"وروى أبو سعيد عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: \" أكثروا ذكر الله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:41"],"words":["ذِكْرًۭا كَثِيرًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"One view calls remembrance abundant when sincere from the heart, and scant when it is merely hypocritical speech on the tongue.","anchor":"وقيل: الذكر الكثير ما جرى على الإخلاص من القلب","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:34:10","rows":[{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَلَقَدْ ءَاتَيْنَا دَاوُۥدَ مِنَّا فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The passage answers deniers of Muhammad's prophethood: sending messengers is not unprecedented; God sent earlier messengers, supported them with miracles, and punished opponents.","anchor":"بين لمنكري نبوة محمد صلى الله عليه وسلم أن إرسال الرسل ليس أمرا بدعا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["ءَاتَيْنَا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Ātaynā means ‘We gave.’","anchor":"آتينا } أعطينا. { فضلا }","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Faḍlan means something by which God favored David above others.","anchor":"فضلا } أي أمرا فضلناه به على غيره","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"The first of nine reported explanations of David's special favor is prophethood.","anchor":"واختلف في هذا الفضل على تسعة أقوال: الأول: النبوة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"The second reported explanation of the special favor is the Psalter.","anchor":"الأول: النبوة. الثاني: الزبور","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"A third explanation is knowledge, as in the verse saying God gave David and Solomon knowledge.","anchor":"الثالث: العلم، قال الله تعالى: ولقد آتينا داود وسليمان علما","mentions":["27:15"]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"A fourth explanation is strength, supported by the description of David as possessing strength.","anchor":"الرابع: القوة، قال الله تعالى: واذكر عبدنا داود ذا الأيد","mentions":["38:17"]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"A fifth explanation is that the mountains and people were subjected to David.","anchor":"الخامس: تسخير الجبال والناس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"A sixth explanation is David's repentance and forgiveness.","anchor":"السادس: التوبة، قال الله تعالى: فغفرنا له ذلك","mentions":["38:25"]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"A seventh explanation is judgment with justice, supported by the address appointing David as vicegerent on earth.","anchor":"السابع: الحكم بالعدل، قال الله تعالى","mentions":["38:26"]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"An eighth explanation is the softening of iron for David.","anchor":"الثامن: إلانة الحديد، قال تعالى: { وألنا له الحديد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"A ninth explanation is David's beautiful voice; the passage also describes his face as beautiful.","anchor":"التاسع: حسن الصوت، وكان داود عليه السلام ذا صوت حسن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The author treats beautiful voice as God's gift and connects it with ‘He increases creation as He wills.’","anchor":"وحسن الصوت هبة من الله تعالى وتفضل منه","mentions":["35:1"]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"The Prophet told Abu Musa that he had been given one of the flutes of David's family, praising his voice.","anchor":"قال صلى الله عليه وسلم لأبي موسى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"العلماء","stance":"reports","claim":"Scholars explain mizmar and mizmūr as a beautiful voice; the instrument is named mizmar for its sound.","anchor":"قال العلماء: المزمار والمزمور الصوت الحسن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["فَضْلًۭا"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Many jurists approve beautifying and melodically varying Qur'an recitation; the author says he discussed this in the introduction.","anchor":"وقد استحسن كثير من فقهاء الأمصار القراءة بالتزيين والترجيع","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["يَٰٓجِبَالُ أَوِّبِى مَعَهُۥ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The command means God told the mountains to repeat glorification with David, as another verse says they glorified with him at evening and sunrise.","anchor":"أي وقلنا يا جبال أوبي معه، أي سبحي معه","mentions":["38:18"]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["أَوِّبِى"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"أبو ميسرة","stance":"reports","claim":"Abu Maysara says the word is Ethiopian for glorification.","anchor":"قال أبو ميسرة: هو التسبيح بلسان الحبشة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["يَٰٓجِبَالُ أَوِّبِى مَعَهُۥ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The mountains' glorification means God created it in them as He created speech in a tree, making their audible response a miracle for David.","anchor":"ومعنى تسبيح الجبال: هو أن الله تعالى خلق فيها تسبيحا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["أَوِّبِى مَعَهُۥ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"Another interpretation is to travel with David during the day's full journey and stop when night comes.","anchor":"وقيل: المعنى سيري معه حيث شاء من التأويب","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:34:10#2","rows":[{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["أَوِّبِى مَعَهُۥ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"ابن مقبل","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Muqbil's line uses awbū al-sayr for completing a day's journey, supporting the travel interpretation.","anchor":"لحقنا بحي أوبوا السير بعدما","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["أَوِّبِى"],"type":"readings","speaker":"الحسن وقتادة وغيرهما","stance":"reports","claim":"Hasan, Qatada, and others read awib with the sense ‘return with him,’ from the verb āba, to return.","anchor":"وقرأ الحسن وقتادة وغيرهما: «أوبي معه» أي رجعي معه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["أَوِّبِى مَعَهُۥ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"A further interpretation is that mountains move with David through the day as he moves; when he recites the Psalter, mountains sound with him and birds listen.","anchor":"وقيل: المعنى تصرفي معه على ما يتصرف عليه داود بالنهار","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["أَوِّبِى مَعَهُۥ وَٱلطَّيْرَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"وهب بن منبه","stance":"reports","claim":"Wahb says the mountains echoed David's lamenting call and birds gathered above; their support strengthened his voice whenever he faltered.","anchor":"وقال وهب بن منبه: المعنى نوحي معه والطير تساعده","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["أَوِّبِى مَعَهُۥ وَٱلطَّيْرَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"وهب بن منبه","stance":"reports","claim":"Wahb adds that David's voice was so beautiful that wild animals gathered and flowing water stopped to listen.","anchor":"وكان قد أعطي من الصوت ما يتزاحم الوحوش من الجبال","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:34:10#3","rows":[{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَٱلطَّيْرَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"ابن أبي إسحاق ونصر عن عاصم وابن هرمز ومسلمة بن عبد الملك","stance":"reports","claim":"These readers use the nominative, coordinating with the word mountains or the pronoun in awibi; separation by maʿa makes the latter possible.","anchor":"«والطير» بالرفع قراءة ابن أبي إسحاق ونصر عن عاصم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَٱلطَّيْرَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"سيبويه","stance":"reports","claim":"The other readers use the accusative, which Sibawayh parses as coordination with the grammatical position of the vocative yā-jibāl.","anchor":"الباقون بالنصب عطفا على موضع «يا جبال» أي نادينا الجبال","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَٱلطَّيْرَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"أبو عمرو بن العلاء","stance":"reports","claim":"Abu Amr ibn al-Ala parses the accusative by supplying an implicit verb meaning ‘We subjected the birds to him.’","anchor":"وعند أبي عمرو بن العلاء بإضمار فعل على معنى وسخرنا له الطير","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَٱلطَّيْرَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الكسائي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Kisaʾi connects the word to ‘We gave David,’ meaning that God also gave him the birds.","anchor":"وقال الكسائي: هو معطوف، أي وآتيناه الطير","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَٱلطَّيْرَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"النحاس","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Nahhas says the word can be an object of accompaniment, like saying the water and the log floated together.","anchor":"مفعولا معه، كما تقول: استوى الماء والخشبة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَٱلطَّيْرَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الزجاج","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Zajjaj allows coordination like ‘I stood with Zayd’; the meaning is that the mountains and birds glorify with David.","anchor":"وسمعت الزجاج يجيز: قمت وزيدا، فالمعنى أوبي معه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلْحَدِيدَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas says iron became like wax in David's hand.","anchor":"قال ابن عباس: صار عنده كالشمع","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلْحَدِيدَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Hasan says the iron became like dough, so David could shape it without fire.","anchor":"وقال الحسن: كالعجين، فكان يعمله من غير نار","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلْحَدِيدَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"السدي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Suddi says iron was like wet clay, dough, or wax and could be shaped without fire or hammering.","anchor":"وقال السدي: كان الحديد في يده كالطين المبلول والعجين والشمع","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلْحَدِيدَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"مقاتل","stance":"reports","claim":"Muqatil says David could finish a coat of armor in part of a day or night, valued at one thousand dirhams.","anchor":"مقاتل: وكان يفرغ من الدرع في بعض اليوم أو بعض الليل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلْحَدِيدَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"An account says David went out in disguise to learn what Israelites thought of him and met a king whom he took for a man; the king said he lived from the treasury.","anchor":"وقيل: أعطي قوة يثني بها الحديد، وسبب ذلك أن داود","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلْحَدِيدَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"In the account, the king says David's virtues would be complete if he earned his living by hand; David asks God to teach and ease a craft and is taught armor making.","anchor":"فقال له الملك «نعم العبد لولا خلة فيه» قال داود","mentions":["21:80"]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلْحَدِيدَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The account says David made armor worth a thousand dirhams per day, supported his household and the poor, spent a third on public needs, and was first to make armor, previously made as plates.","anchor":"فكان يصنع الدرع فيما بين يومه وليلته يساوي ألف درهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلْحَدِيدَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"قيل","stance":"reports","claim":"A further report says David sold each coat of armor for four thousand dirhams.","anchor":"ويقال: إنه كان يبيع كل درع منها بأربعة آلاف","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلْحَدِيدَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Dirʿ is feminine for armor used in war, but masculine for a woman's breastplate.","anchor":"والدرع مؤنثة إذا كانت للحرب. ودرع المرأة مذكر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلْحَدِيدَ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The verse supports people of excellence learning crafts: work adds humility, independence, and lawful earnings without indebtedness to others.","anchor":"في هذه الآية دليل على تعلم أهل الفضل الصنائع","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:34:10#4","rows":[{"verses":["34:10"],"words":["وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلْحَدِيدَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"النبي","stance":"reports","claim":"The Prophet said the best food a person eats is from his own labor, and that David, God's prophet, ate from his own labor.","anchor":"إن خير ما أكل المرء من عمل يده وإن نبي الله داود كان يأكل من عمل يده","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:34:11","rows":[{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["أَنِ ٱعْمَلْ سَٰبِغَٰتٍۢ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Sābighāt are complete, full, spacious coats of armor; the root describes something covering the body and extending beyond it.","anchor":"أي دروعا سابغات، أي كوامل تامات واسعات","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["وَقَدِّرْ فِى ٱلسَّرْدِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Qatada says earlier armor was heavy plates, so David was told to balance lightness with protection.","anchor":"قال قتادة: كانت الدروع قبله صفائح فكانت ثقالا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["وَقَدِّرْ فِى ٱلسَّرْدِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن زيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Zayd says the measure concerns ring size: rings must not be so small that the armor is weak or so large that they harm the wearer.","anchor":"وقال ابن زيد: التقدير الذي مر به هو في قدر الحلقة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["وَقَدِّرْ فِى ٱلسَّرْدِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Abbas says the measure concerns rivets: a thin one loosens the links and a thick one splits them; the text reports alternate verbs.","anchor":"وقال ابن عباس: التقدير الذي أمر به هو في المسمار","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["ٱلسَّرْدِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Sard is the weaving of armor rings; its maker is called sarād or zarād, with sīn and zāy alternating as in sirāṭ and zirāṭ.","anchor":"في السرد } السرد نسج حلق الدروع ومنه قيل لصانع حلق الدروع: السراد والزراد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["ٱلسَّرْدِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Sard also means sewing: sarada yasrudu means to sew, and a misrad is an awl; sarād can mean the thong used for sewing.","anchor":"والسرد: الخرز، يقال سرد يسرد إذا خرز، والمسرد: الإشفى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["ٱلسَّرْدِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الشماخ","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Shammakh's line uses sard for consecutive stitching of reins, illustrating the sewing sense.","anchor":"قال الشماخ: فظلت تباعا خيلنا في بيوتكم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["ٱلسَّرْدِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Sard also describes speech or fasting done consecutively in an unbroken sequence.","anchor":"ويقال: قد سرد الحديث والصوم فالسرد فيهما أن يجيء بهما","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["ٱلسَّرْدِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عائشة","stance":"reports","claim":"Aisha reports that the Prophet did not speak in a rapid unbroken sequence; he spoke distinctly enough to be counted.","anchor":"وفي حديث عائشة: لم يكن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم يسرد الحديث","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["ٱلسَّرْدِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"سيبويه","stance":"reports","claim":"Sibawayh says sarandā means a bold person because he presses forward; the image derives from armor rings joined in order.","anchor":"قال سيبويه: ومنه رجل سرندى أي جريء، قال: لأنه يمضي قدما","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["ٱلسَّرْدِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"لبيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Labid's line describes iron made with doubled rings, exemplifying mail construction.","anchor":"قال لبيد: صنع الحديد مضاعفا أسراده","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["ٱلسَّرْدِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"أبو ذؤيب","stance":"reports","claim":"Abu Dhuʾayb describes two garments of mail made by David or a Tubbaʿ, using masrūdatān for linked armor.","anchor":"وقال أبو ذؤيب: وعليهما مسرودتان قضاهما داود","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:34:11#2","rows":[{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["وَٱعْمَلُوا۟ صَٰلِحًا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The command means to perform righteous deeds and is addressed to David and his household, as in the command to the House of David to work in gratitude.","anchor":"أي عملا صالحا. وهذا خطاب لداود وأهله","mentions":["34:13"]},{"verses":["34:11"],"words":["إِنِّى بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌۭ"],"type":"theology","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"God sees what they do.","anchor":"إني بما تعملون بصير","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:35:18","rows":[{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَلَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌۭ وِزْرَ أُخْرَىٰ"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The commentary says this verse was treated earlier and is detached from what immediately precedes it.","anchor":"تقدم الكلام فيه، وهو مقطوع مما قبله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["تَزِرُ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The underlying form is tawzar; its wāw was deleted to match the form of yazir.","anchor":"والأصل «توزر» حذفت الواو اتباعا ليزر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَازِرَةٌۭ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Wāzirah is an adjective of an elided noun, meaning a burden-bearing soul.","anchor":"نعت لمحذوف، أي نفس وازرة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَإِن تَدْعُ مُثْقَلَةٌ إِلَىٰ حِمْلِهَا"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farraʾ supplies an elided nafs or beast for muthqalah and says the expression applies to masculine or feminine.","anchor":"قال الفراء: أي نفس مثقلة أو دابة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَإِن تَدْعُ مُثْقَلَةٌ إِلَىٰ حِمْلِهَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الأخفش","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Akhfash understands a sin-burdened person to be asking another person to carry her sins.","anchor":"قال الأخفش: أي وإن تدع مثقلة إنسانا إلى حملها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["حِمْلِهَا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الكسائي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Kisaʾi says ḥaml for what is carried on the back, pregnancy, and a date cluster is pronounced with fatḥah only.","anchor":"حكاهما الكسائي بالفتح لا غير","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["حِمْلِهَا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"ابن السكيت","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn al-Sikkit allows the word for a date cluster to be pronounced with either fatḥah or kasrah.","anchor":"وحكى ابن السكيت أن حمل النخلة يفتح ويكسر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["لَا يُحْمَلْ مِنْهُ شَىْءٌۭ وَلَوْ كَانَ ذَا قُرْبَىٰٓ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الأخفش","stance":"reports","claim":"On al-Akhfash's parse, the omitted subject is the person being called upon: even if that person were a close relative, no burden would be carried.","anchor":"التقدير على قول الأخفش: ولو كان الإنسان المدعو ذا قربى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَلَوْ كَانَ ذَا قُرْبَىٰٓ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الفراء وسيبويه","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farraʾ permits the nominative dhū qurbā; Sibawayh accepts it as in 2:280, with kāna meaning ‘occurred’ or with a predicate understood.","anchor":"وهذا جائز عند سيبويه، ومثله { وإن كان ذو عسرة }","mentions":["2:280"]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَلَوْ كَانَ ذَا قُرْبَىٰٓ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"سيبويه","stance":"reports","claim":"Sibawayh gives the elliptical example ‘people are requited for their deeds, if good then good,’ with a second case-form alternative.","anchor":"وحكى سيبويه: الناس مجزيون بأعمالهم إن خير فخير","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَإِن تَدْعُ مُثْقَلَةٌ إِلَىٰ حِمْلِهَا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عكرمة","stance":"reports","claim":"Ikrima relays that at the Resurrection a Jew or Christian asks a Muslim to help because of past kindness; the Muslim asks God until some punishment is reduced.","anchor":"وروي عن عكرمة أنه قال: بلغني أن اليهودي والنصراني يرى الرجل المسلم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["لَا يُحْمَلْ مِنْهُ شَىْءٌۭ وَلَوْ كَانَ ذَا قُرْبَىٰٓ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عكرمة","stance":"reports","claim":"Ikrima's report continues with parents, children, and spouses refusing requests to transfer a good deed or bear a sin because they fear their own judgment.","anchor":"وأن الرجل ليأتي إلى أبيه يوم القيامة فيقول: ألم أكن بك بارا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَإِن تَدْعُ مُثْقَلَةٌ إِلَىٰ حِمْلِهَا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"الفضيل بن عياض","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Fudayl ibn ʿIyad pictures a mother reminding her child of pregnancy, nursing, and care, then asking him to carry one sin; he refuses, occupied with his own sin.","anchor":"فتقول: يا ولدي، ألم يكن بطني لك وعاء، ألم يكن ثديي لك سقاء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["إِنَّمَا تُنذِرُ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخْشَوْنَ رَبَّهُم بِٱلْغَيْبِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The warning is accepted by those who fear God's punishment, as in the verse about those who follow the Reminder and fear the Merciful unseen.","anchor":"أي إنما يقبل إنذارك من يخشى عقاب الله تعالى","mentions":["36:11"]}]}
{"loc":"QURTUBI-FULL:35:18#2","rows":[{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَمَن تَزَكَّىٰ فَإِنَّمَا يَتَزَكَّىٰ لِنَفْسِهِۦ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Whoever purifies himself is guided for his own benefit.","anchor":"أي من اهتدى فإنما يهتدي لنفسه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَمَن تَزَكَّىٰ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A variant reads man izzakkā fa-innamā yazzakkā li-nafsih, using forms of purifying oneself.","anchor":"وقرىء: «ومن ازكى فإنما يزكى لنفسه»","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَإِلَى ٱللَّهِ ٱلْمَصِيرُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"All creation returns to God.","anchor":"وإلى الله المصير } أي إليه مرجع جميع الخلق","mentions":[]}]}
